course: dictionary
lesson: 7431
title: Pollen: a flower's dust with a job
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Pollen is a fine yellow powder made by flowers. A plant needs pollen to make seeds, and pollen has to travel from one flower to another, carried by insects or the wind.
explain: The sentences give you clues. «On a sunny day a honeybee lands on a flower, drinks sweet nectar... and flies off with yellow balls of pollen packed on its back legs.» The bee is carrying pollen like a shopper carries bags, so pollen is something that can be carried.
explain: Look at this one: «Itchy red eyes every spring are usually pollen allergy.» Here pollen is something in the air that can make you sneeze and itch. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Pollen is a noun, and it is uncountable, so we say some pollen, not two pollens.
fact: «Pollination» means pollen moving from one flower to another, so that seeds and fruit can grow.
fact: Bees collect pollen as food and carry it on their legs.
fact: Pollen in the air can cause hay fever, with sneezing and itchy eyes, especially in spring and summer.
fact: A «pollen count» on the weather report tells you how much pollen is in the air.
exercise: «On a sunny day a honeybee... flies off with yellow balls of pollen packed on its back legs.» Where does the bee carry the pollen? | *On its back legs | In its wings | Under its tail | In its tongue
exercise: What is pollen? | A kind of seed that grows into a tree | A sweet liquid that bees drink | *A fine yellow powder made by flowers | A small insect that lives on flowers
exercise: Pollen must be carried from one flower to another. What carries it? | Cars and buses | Rain and snow | Stones and soil | *Insects or the wind
test: Why does a plant need pollen? | To make its leaves turn green | *To help it make seeds | To keep it warm in winter | To attract fish to its roots
test: Itchy red eyes every spring are usually caused by what? | Cold water on your face | Too much sunshine on your skin | A germ you catch from a friend | *Pollen in the air
exam: «Lilies are very poisonous to cats; even pollen licked off their fur can damage the kidneys.» What does this tell us? | Lilies have no pollen at all | *Pollen from lilies can harm a cat if it is licked off the fur | Pollen is harmless to every animal | Cats love to eat pollen
